  "description": "LUXTEF crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C64 H80 Eu4 N4 O20,C1 H4 O1. From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu4 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.737-3.983 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.36-112.04°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C65H84Eu4N4O21. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
